  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": "B00",
      "act": "ASK",
      "narration_text": "Hi, I am Saurabh K., and this video is about A I agents that act on their own. What that actually means, and where the limits have to come from. One note first. The voice you are hearing is A I generated. The work and the evidence are mine. Here is the question.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "Hello, HAI",
            "topic": "Irreducibly Human",
            "segment": "Agents, On Their Own",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "command": "Everyone says AI agents now act on their own. What does that actually mean in the software, and if it really decides its own next step, what stops it?"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B00.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-18T23:15:46.242715+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 20,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B00.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.99,
      "render_duration_s": 14.0,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B00.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk",
        "at": "2026-10-18T23:54:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "BLUF",
      "narration_text": "The short version first. An agent is not a smarter model. It is the same model put inside a loop, and given the ability to act in between the turns. Nothing about that loop knows when to stop. That part is still ours, and it has to be written down.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "BrutalistHesitantWriter",
          "props": {
            "text": "An agent is a smarter model.\nNo, it is the same model\nput inside a loop, and given\nhands between the turns.\nThe stopping is still ours.",
            "face": "serif",
            "align": "center",
            "fontSize": 160,
            "lineSpacing": 1.16,
            "charMs": 18,
            "hesitateBetween": 0,
            "hesitateWithin": 0,
            "mistakeRate": 0,
            "jitter": 5
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-18T23:16:37.478803+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 18,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.65,
      "render_duration_s": 13.666666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:BrutalistHesitantWriter",
        "at": "2026-10-18T23:54:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "WHAT",
      "narration_text": "So what changes. A plain model answers once and waits for you. Put it in a loop and the pause disappears. It reads what came back from its own last action, picks the next one, and goes again. Nobody is being asked in between. That gap is the whole thing people mean by acting on its own.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeTldrWhat",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "LOOP",
            "greeting": "Hello, HAI",
            "topic": "Irreducibly Human",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "heading": "The pause is what disappears",
            "question": "What makes it an agent?",
            "lines": [
              "A model answers, then waits",
              "An agent reads what it got",
              "and picks the next step itself"
            ],
            "durationSeconds": 15.27
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-19T02:36:45.505397+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.27,
      "render_duration_s": 15.291666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeTldrWhat",
        "at": "2026-10-18T23:54:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "TERMS",
      "narration_text": "Four words that carry the weight. A tool is one thing it is allowed to do. A loop is it choosing the next one by itself. Autonomy is just how many of those turns happen without you. And a guardrail is a rule the software enforces whether or not the model agrees with it.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeDefinitions",
          "props": {
            "title": "Four terms",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "terms": [
              {
                "term": "Tool",
                "meaning": "One thing it is allowed to do"
              },
              {
                "term": "Loop",
                "meaning": "It picks the next step itself"
              },
              {
                "term": "Autonomy",
                "meaning": "How many turns happen without you"
              },
              {
                "term": "Guardrail",
                "meaning": "A rule the software enforces anyway"
              }
            ],
            "durationSeconds": 14.61
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-19T03:52:51.902312+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.61,
      "render_duration_s": 14.625,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeDefinitions",
        "at": "2026-10-18T23:54:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "EVIDENCE",
      "narration_text": "Here is a real one, from this machine today. A long job was handed off to run by itself. It kept going with nobody watching, and when it finished it came back and said so. That is an agent turn that happened entirely without a person in it.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "task-event.json",
            "language": "json",
            "sparkLine": "It ran, and reported back.",
            "code": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"bvg1cuail\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Background command\n     'Run the full compile' completed\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0\n}"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-18T23:18:25.319697+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 20,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.59,
      "render_duration_s": 13.625,
      "build": {
