        "at": "2026-10-18T23:54:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "GUARDRAIL",
      "narration_text": "And here is the guardrail that came attached to it, word for word. The system tells the agent that this event is not a person speaking. Do not read it as permission. Somebody anticipated that a machine hearing its own echo might mistake it for consent, and wrote the rule down in advance.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "guardrail.txt",
            "language": "text",
            "sparkLine": "An echo is not consent.",
            "code": "This is an automated background-task\nevent, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user\nacknowledgement, confirmation, or\nresponse to any pending question.",
            "largeText": true
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-19T02:42:23.963115+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.49,
      "render_duration_s": 15.5,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeCodeBeat",
        "at": "2026-10-18T23:54:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "REFUSAL",
      "narration_text": "The second kind of limit is a refusal. Making the last video, the toolkit stopped me six separate times. Missing paperwork. Text outside the safe area. A glyph too small to read. It could not judge whether the film was any good. It could check the things a human had already decided mattered, and it would not move until they passed.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "gate-refusals.log",
            "language": "bash",
            "sparkLine": "It stopped itself.",
            "code": "$ art final hai-mcp-explained\nREFUSED  GATE F  FACTCHECK.md missing\nexit=2\n$ art final hai-mcp-explained\nFAIL     GATE T  overflow B02 x0=188\nexit=2\n$ art run    hai-mcp-explained\nBLOCKER  gate-v  edge-bleed B01_85\nexit=2"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-18T23:25:31.005767+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 24,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.94,
      "render_duration_s": 16.958333333333332,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeCodeBeat",
        "at": "2026-10-18T23:54:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "JUDGE",
      "narration_text": "So when should you let one run. When the work is checkable, when a mistake is cheap to undo, and when a rule can be written down ahead of time. Be careful the moment it is none of those. The honest test is simple. If you cannot say what would make it stop, it is not ready to run on its own.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeTldrWhy",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "WHEN",
            "topic": "Irreducibly Human",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "heading": "Name the stop condition first",
            "lead": "Let it run when the work is checkable.",
            "lines": [
              "LET IT RUN — undo is cheap",
              "LOOK TWICE — nothing checks it",
              "No stop condition? Then stop"
            ],
            "durationSeconds": 14.7
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B07.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-19T02:43:03.025738+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 24,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.7,
      "render_duration_s": 14.708333333333334,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeTldrWhy",
        "at": "2026-10-18T23:54:48"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "YOUR-TURN",
      "narration_text": "Your turn. Take whichever A I tool you already let run by itself, and before you start it again, write one sentence. What would have to happen for this to stop. If you cannot finish that sentence, you have found the thing to fix first.",
